IV. EXPERIMENTS RESULTS
A. Datasets
1) Collected Datasets: Our team collected activity data from 51 healthy volunteers and 51 PD patients at a hospital between November 18, 2023, and July 21, 2024. During the data collection process, Shimmer3 IMU sensors were worn on the left wrist, right wrist, left ankle, right ankle, and waist to capture accelerometer, gyroscope, and magnetometer signals. Each participant was instructed to perform 16 designated activities, with a 1-minute rest period between each task. A detailed description of these activities is available in work [10]. For simplicity and to enhance compliance, we use only data from the left and right wrist sensors, and focus specifically on the wrist-flip activity based on Zhao’s findings [28]. 2) Public Datasets: To further evaluate the effectiveness of our model, we also used two publicly available datasets: PADS [17]: The PADS dataset collects activity data from participants using two smartwatches and a smartphone. The
